>
> My questions:
>
> =A0* Are the cases I point about above errors in camxes?

No, that's the intent. It's supposed to look at the following
construction and erase back to a construction of the same type, or
even just the start of one.

>=A0 Is "Magic
> =A0 Words" the most authoritative description of SA or did that
> =A0 change and camxes is doing something it should be?

Define "authoritative". The BPFK hasn't made any firm decision on what
SA should do, and CLL has more than one different descriptions of what
it is suppposed to do.

> =A0* do the words |...| in |selma'o ... si selma'o| need to be
> =A0 grammatical by themselves? =A0Or just lojbanic words? =A0What about
> =A0 non-lojbanic words?

I don't think it needs to be grammatical, since the idea is that you
can correct mistakes with it. I think camxes does require them to be
Lojban words, but that's not necessarily the best idea.

